# kindle-launchpad — Neo's KindleLaunch autonomy skill (MatrixScript manifest).
# Companion prose body lives in SKILL.md and carries the same anti-fake +
# key-isolation mandate. Teaches the MCL planner the procedures behind the five
# KindleLaunch capabilities so a core_execute intent plans + runs them:
#   LAUNCH  — Router.createMarket (+ USDL creation-fee approve, optical, metadata)
#   TRADE   — buy / sell / swapTokenForToken, quote-bounded min-out + deadline
#   COLLECT — FeesRouter NFT-owner-gated fee actions (claim/burn/airdrop/lp)
#   WATCH   — chronos alarm_set -> wake -> re-read -> triggered core_execute
#   OPTICAL — preset attach/deploy, or BaseOptical-derived custom via Tachyon
#
# KEY ISOLATION (frozen backstop_1): this skill NEVER holds a signing key. Every
# value-moving step is a kindle WRITE tool whose calldata is signed + broadcast
# SERVER-SIDE by the per-user embedded wallet (/v1/agent/* lane) under the
# user's one-time leash (mode + spend caps). A wallet 403 (frozen / wrong mode /
# over cap) is a CLEAN denial surfaced in plain language — never retried as
# transient. All amount/price/slippage/fee math is integer base-unit math
# (USDL = 6 decimals; launched tokens = 18 unless they report otherwise).

§SKILL
id=kindle-launchpad
version=0.1.0
display="KindleLaunch Autonomy"
author=did:pax:0xMATRIX
description="Launch, trade, watch, collect fees, and create opticals on KindleLaunch (the Sidiora launchpad on Paxeer Network, chain 125). LAUNCH a token + market via Router.createMarket (USDL creation-fee approve, fee strategy CLAIM|BURN|AIRDROP|LP_REWARDS, optional optical, and display metadata so it renders on the frontend). TRADE with buy/sell/swapTokenForToken, deriving every minimum-out from a real Quoter read and an explicit slippage tolerance via integer base-unit math with a finite deadline. COLLECT a pool's fees through the FeesRouter, NFT-owner gated and matched to the pool's current strategy. WATCH a pool/position/fee balance on a schedule via the chronos scheduler, re-reading state on wake and dispatching the trade or fee action through core_execute only when the trigger condition is met. CREATE OPTICALS in two tiers: attach a deployed preset (anti-snipe, max-wallet, tax, cooldown, buyback-burn), or author a BaseOptical-derived custom optical and compile/test/deploy it through the shared Tachyon engine (forge). Every value-moving call is signed server-side by the per-user embedded wallet under a one-time leash (mode + spend caps); this skill holds no key and a wallet 403 is surfaced as a plain-language denial, never retried. Verbs: build = launch a market or create an optical; acquire = trade or collect fees; monitor = watch; analyze = read pools/markets/quotes/fees/opticals. Every claimed outcome is grounded in a real tool result (a tx hash, a quote, a balance, an explorer link); nothing is reported done without it."
mcl.verbs=build acquire monitor analyze
determinism=seedable
seed_policy=per_intent

§INPUTS
slot target: ArtifactRef
  required
  hint="The KindleLaunch task in the user's words. LAUNCH (create a token/market, with name/symbol/fee-strategy and optionally an optical + display metadata), TRADE (buy/sell/swap a token with a size + slippage), COLLECT (claim/route a pool's fees), WATCH (monitor a pool/position/fee balance on a schedule until a condition, then act), or OPTICAL (attach a preset, or describe a custom pool behavior to build + deploy). May name a pool/token address or symbol, an NFT id, a fee strategy, an optical preset or behavior, a schedule/condition, or a size + slippage."

slot constraints: Constraint[]
  optional
  hint="Bounds on the work: max spend (USDL/PAX), slippage tolerance (bps), which pools/tokens are in scope, dry-run vs execute, the wallet leash mode (read_only|trade_only|full) the user has granted, and watch cadence/expiry. The embedded wallet enforces mode + spend caps server-side; these are the in-plan bounds Matrix reads before dispatching."

§CORTEX
reads=Identity Constraint Capability Goal Event Fact
tags=kindle kindlelaunch sidiora launchpad paxeer chain125 launch trade buy sell swap fees optical watch monitor router quoter feesrouter feeaccumulator opticalregistry usdl embedded wallet leash tachyon chronos build acquire monitor analyze

§TOOLS
# ── KindleLaunch reads (Neo-callable; no signing) ─────────────────────────
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_pools@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_market@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_quote@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_fees@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_optical_info@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_position@0.1.0
# ── KindleLaunch writes (escalate-class; embedded wallet signs server-side) ─
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_launch@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_set_metadata@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_buy@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_sell@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_swap@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_collect_fees@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_set_fee_strategy@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_create_optical_preset@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/kindle/kindle_create_optical_custom@0.1.0
# ── CONTRACTS · custom optical compile/test/deploy via the Tachyon engine ──
matrix://tool/mcp/tachyon/tachyon_compile@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/tachyon/tachyon_test@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/tachyon/tachyon_simulate@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/tachyon/tachyon_deploy@0.1.0
matrix://tool/mcp/tachyon/tachyon_call@0.1.0
